uctoisomerase (DXR) is an enzyme involved in the first step in the nonmevalonate pathway for isoprenoid biosynthesis in Gram-negative, Gram-positive bacteria, plants, and the parasite causing the most virulent form of malaria, Plasmodium falciparum (Mammals produce isoprenoids via the mevalonate pathway).\nL212: \nL213: * * *\nL214: ## Compare Similar Items\nL215: \nL216: 【16†View Full Comparison】\nL217: \nL218: * * *\nL219: \nL220: Show Differences\nL221: \nL222: [Input]\nL223: \nL224: 1 of 1\nL225: ###### This Item\nL226:  | F8307  | N1876  | N5285\nL227: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL228: 【17†Sigma-Aldrich F8682 Fosmidomycin sodium salt hydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【18†Sigma-Aldrich F8307 FR-900098 monosodium salt】[Button: Quick View]  | 【19†Sigma-Aldrich N1876 Neomycin trisulfate salt hydrate】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich N5285 Neomycin trisulfate salt hydrate】[Button: Quick View]\nL229: description≥95% (NMR)  | description≥97% (NMR)  | description powder  | description meets USP testing specifications, powder\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nD-(+)-Melezitose =97 HPLC 207511-10-2 (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/m5375)\nciteturn96view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/m5375\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 387\nL0: 【0†Skip to Content】\nL1: \nL2: Products\nL3: \nL4: [Input]\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Type in Product Names, Product Numbers, or CAS Numbers to see suggestions.]\nL7: \nL8: Cart 0\nL9: \nL10: US EN\nL11: \nL12: Products\nL13: \nL14: [Input]\nL15: \nL16: [Input: Type in Product Names, Product Numbers, or CAS Numbers to see suggestions.]\nL17: \nL18: Products Applications Services Resources Support\nL19: \nL20: 【1†Login / Register】\nL21: \nL22: 【2†Order Lookup】\nL23: \nL24: 【3†Quick Order】\nL25: \nL26: Cart 0\nL27: \nL28: 【4†Products】\nL29: \nL30: 【5†Biochemicals】\nL31: \nL32: M5