5% trace metals basis\nL156: \nL157: ### form\nL158: \nL159: crystals and lumps\nL160: \nL161: ### composition\nL162: \nL163: Degree of hydration, ~3\nL164: \nL165: ### reaction suitability\nL166: \nL167: core: gold, reagent type: inorganic catalyst\nL168: \nL169: ### technique(s)\nL170: \nL171: ELISA: suitable\nL172: \nL173: ### impurities\nL174: \nL175: ≤55.0 ppm Trace Metal Analysis\nL176: \nL177: ### density\nL178: \nL179: 3.9 g/mL at 25 °C\nL180: \nL181: ### SMILES string\nL182: \nL183: O.Cl.Cl[Au](Cl)Cl\nL184: \nL185: ### InChI\nL186: \nL187: 1S/Au.4ClH.H2O/h;4*1H;1H2/q+3;;;;;/p-3\nL188: \nL189: ### InChI key\nL190: \nL191: OVJUDSKPNIBLOO-UHFFFAOYSA-K\nL192: \nL193: Description\nL194: ### General description\nL195: \nL196: Gold (III) chloride hydrate (HAuCl_{4}) can be used as a precursor to synthesize goldnanoparticles and p-type dopant for most conjugated organic molecules. Thedoping leads to the expansion of crystalline lattice and enhances conductivitydue to the formation of a large number of chargecarriers.\nL197: ### Application\nL198: Gold(III) chloride hydrate can be used to prepare TiO_{2}-supported Au-based photocatalyst by deposition-precipitation with urea. These catalysts show a higher amount and production rate of hydrogen via a water-splitting reaction.\nL199: Conjugate polythiophene films can be prepared by the solution-doping method using HAuCl_{4} as a dopant. These highly conductive polymer films can be applied in the field of vapor sensing and organic electronics.\nL200: HAuCl_{4} can be reduced to prepare gold nanoparticles by using different reducing agents like NaBH_{4}, glucose, and poly (propylene imine) dendrimer.\nL201: * * *\nL202: ## Compare Similar Items\nL203: \nL204: 【17†View Full Comparison】\nL205: \nL206: * * *\nL207: \nL208: Show Differences\nL209: \nL210: [Input]\nL211: \nL212: 1 of 1\nL213: ###### This Item\nL214:  | 50780  | 50790  | 484385\nL215: --- | --- | --- | ---\n"
